# Exercise 4: OR
#
# Sometimes either of two things is enough. Join the goals with OR:
#
#     rule can_enter(x):
#         has_ticket(x)
#         OR is_staff(x)
#
# Sova tries each side, and each one that works gives an answer.
#
# Your task: write family(x, y), which is true when x is a parent of y,
# or y is a parent of x.

fact parent("Ada", "Ben")
fact parent("Ben", "Cy")

# Write your rule below this line.



# --- Checks: run ./sova --check on this file. Don't change below here. ---
hint "Write two goals joined by OR: one where x is the parent, and one where y is."
hint "parent(x, y) OR parent(y, x)"
expect family("Ada", "Ben")
expect family("Ben", "Ada")
expect family("Cy", "Ben")
expect NOT family("Ada", "Cy")
expect family("Ben", who) gives "Ada", "Cy"
